  note          = {Cited by: 0},
  abstract      = {It is now possible to produce ready mixed concrete with strengths of 75 to 150 MPa with slumps of 180-100 mm, as well as fluid 200 MPa pre-cast concretes. While in some areas it is difficult to find a cement/superplasticizer combination that is compatible and robust enough to produce a 75 MPa HPC, in other areas it is relatively easy to reach 150 MPa. This is because cement producers optimize the strength of their cements rather than their rheological behaviour in combination with a superplasticizer. However, if we specify a Type I/II ASTM clinker having a maximum C<sub>3</sub>A content of 6\% and about 0.6\% of soluble alkalis, the resulting HPC will not exhibit any rheological problems.},
