  note          = {Cited by: 0},
  abstract      = {The accelerated adoption of artificial intelligence (AI) has caused a surge in demand for data center capacity--growth projected to triple by 2030.<sup>1</sup> The complex workloads of AI-powered computing mean data centers are shifting toward high-performance compute (HPC) rack densities that often trend toward 50 kW per rack. To keep pace, data center owners must optimize available data hall space, creating higher-density facilities that carry a unique set of challenges when it comes to achieving operational performance and sustainability. This article examines how air-cooled magnetic bearing chillers can enhance energy efficiency, improve water usage effectiveness and support decarbonization in high-density data centers now and in the future. \textcopyright{} ASHRAE.},
