  note          = {Cited by: 0},
  abstract      = {As waste concrete and bricks from demolished constructions can be properly processed to produce artificial aggregates and can be substituted for natural aggregate, this will not only solve the waste problems but also prevent natural resources from over-used. This paper is mainly deals with the properties of high performance concrete (HPC) designed with recycled aggregates which are obtained from construction demolished waste. Results show that HPC containing recycled aggregates can reach 46 (DN group) and 44 (DR group) MPa in the category of compressive strength at 91 days of age. As to concrete resistivity, all specimens can, at least, have 40 k\ensuremath{\Omega} \cdot{} cm at the age of 91 days. Also, results of chloride permeation test show that the readings of concrete mixes are all lower than 2000 coulombs according to ASTM C1202-93.},
