  note          = {Cited by: 0},
  abstract      = {The potential of heat/power cogeneration can be compared to a gigantic domestic energy resource of the same order of magnitude as Germany's total production of primary energy from fossil fuels. Around 80 to 90\% of greenhouse-gas emissions from coal-fired power generating plants can be eliminated by means of a natural gas cogeneration plant, and the emission reduction as per GEMIS still amounts to approx. 70\% even compared to modern combined-cycle (gas and steam-turbine) power generating plants without heat recovery. The prospects for HPC are good, despite the fact that the HPC Act fails by far to fulfill all expectations. Great potentials which must be exploited and expanded by means of active support open up for the gas industry and the manual trades.},
