  year          = 2022,
  journal       = {International Journal of Quantum Chemistry},
  volume        = 122,
  number        = 9,
  doi           = {10.1002/qua.26872},
  url           = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85122259190&doi=10.1002%2Fqua.26872&partnerID=40&md5=ec6699bd350e4ee1cc43cc7d93ffa141},
  note          = {Cited by: 23; All Open Access; Green Open Access; Hybrid Gold Open Access},
  abstract      = {The installation of quantum chemistry software packages is commonly done manually and can be a time-consuming and complicated process. An update of the underlying Linux system requires a reinstallation in many cases and can quietly break software installed on the system. In this paper, we present an approach that allows for an easy installation of quantum chemistry software packages, which is also independent of operating system updates. The use of the Nix package manager allows building software in a reproducible manner, which allows for a reconstruction of the software for later reproduction of scientific results. The build recipes that are provided can be readily used by anyone to avoid complex installation procedures. \textcopyright{} 2022 The Authors. International Journal of Quantum Chemistry published by Wiley Periodicals LLC.},
