  pages         = {1649--1654},
  url           = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84953396724&partnerID=40&md5=b76333433ab2e79655c9fd5a3a45125f},
  note          = {Cited by: 1},
  abstract      = {HPC has undergone many growths based on the persuade of cement type, type and proportions of mineral admixtures, type of superplasticiser and the mineralogical composition of coarse and fine aggregates. The constituent materials of HPC depend on the desired characteristics and the availability of suitable local economic alternatives. In this study reported on the flexural behavior of high-performance reinforced concrete columns made with manufactured sand and natural coarse aggregate together with silica fume and fly ash. The Columns were made from concrete having compressive strength of 60 N/mm2.An experimental investigation was carried out to understand the structural behavior of reinforced concrete GHPRC columns of size 1000mm x 100 mm x 100mm. This paper presents the load deflection characteristics of GHPRC concrete made with silica fume and fly ash with M-Sand compared with conventional concrete mix. Maximum ultimate load carrying capacity and the least deflection is obtained for the mix prepared by partial replacement of cement with 10\% silica fume \&  15 \% Fly ash with M-Sand. The mineral fillers in M- Sand and ternary blenders increased the flexural stiffness of HPC column. The test results showed that it is possible to produce HPC using M-Sand with silica fume and Fly ash. \textcopyright{} 2015 CAFET-INNOVA TECHNICAL SOCIETY. All rights reserved.},
  author_keywords = {Deflection; Fly ash; Green high-performance reinforced concrete; M-Sand; Reinforced concrete; Silica fume},
