  note          = {Cited by: 2; All Open Access; Gold Open Access; Green Open Access},
  abstract      = {Due to the increase of data volumes expected for the LHC Run 3 and Run 4, the ALICE Collaboration designed and deployed a new, energy efficient, computing model to run Online and Offline (Formula presented.) data processing within a single software framework. The ALICE (Formula presented.) Event Processing Nodes (EPN) project performs online data reconstruction using GPUs (Graphic Processing Units) instead of CPUs and applies an efficient, entropy-based, online data compression to cope with Pb–Pb collision data at a 50 kHz hadronic interaction rate. Also, the (Formula presented.) EPN farm infrastructure features an energy efficient, environmentally friendly, adiabatic cooling system which allows for operational and capital cost savings. Copyright \textcopyright{} 2025 Ronchetti, Akishina, Andreassen, Bluhme, Dange, de Cuveland, Erba, Gaur, Hutter, Kozlov, Kr\v{c}\'{a}l, La Pointe, Lehrbach, Lindenstruth, Ne\v{s}kovi\'{c}, Redelbach, Rohr, Weiglhofer and Wilhelmi.},
