  url           = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-79953683120&partnerID=40&md5=44819eed3febf96e9afad2d4b5b392c6},
  note          = {Cited by: 1},
  abstract      = {High performance computing (HPC) professionals in the US and around the world are making efforts to improve environmentally-friendliness of such computing efforts. A study commissioned by the US Environmental Protection Agency estimates that power consumption by servers has doubled between 2000 and 2005 worldwide and that the total amount of electricity consumed by servers worldwide costs about US \$7.2 billion. An international panel of experts addresses the issues of what are the power limitations of the existing technology in a discussion entitled 'The Greening of HPC - Will Power Consumption Become the Limiting Factor for Future Growth of HPC'?. These experts have also shared their views on the way the situation can be changed to assure the future rapid growth of HPC performance without contributing more to carbon emissions and global warming.},
