  note          = {Cited by: 0},
  abstract      = {SmartTruck, Greenville, S.C., with the help of BMI Corp., Greenville, noted for its application of aerospace aerodynamic technology, has developed trailer drag-reduction devices that are an alternative to conventional trailer skirts and boat tail appendages. SmartTruck's core product is the UnderTray System, which consists of up to four devices designed to reduce drag and improve the aerodynamics of long-haul trailers. The SmartTruck system reduces drag by compressing and accelerating incoming airflow, then injecting high-energy air into the trailer wake. The Cray XT-5 Jaguar supercomputer with a theoretical peak computational capability of 2.3 petaflops allowed SmartTruck to go from a concept to a design ready for manufacture in 18 months, instead of the three and a half years that were originally anticipated.},
